<title>UK: HORSE RACING-AINTREE GRAND NATIONAL RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-AINTREE GRAND NATIONAL RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL, England 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the Aintree</p>
<p>Grand National steeplechase run over four miles and four</p>
<p>furlongs (7.2 kms) on Monday:</p>
<p> 1. Lord Gyllene	14-1 (ridden by Tony Dobbin)</p>
<p> 2. Suny Bay	     8-1 (Jamie Osborne)</p>
<p> 3. Camelot Knight   100-1 (Carl Llewellyn)</p>
<p>4. Buckboard Bounce  40-1 (Paul Carberry)</p>
<p>36 ran.</p>
<p>Non-runners: Belmont King, Master Boston, Plastic Spaceage</p>
<p>and Over The Stream.</p>
<p>Favourite: Go Ballistic, 7-1</p>
<p>Winner owned by Stanley Clarke and trained in England by</p>
<p>Steve Brookshaw</p>
<p>Value to winning owner: 178,000 pounds sterling ($291,000)</p>
</text>
